    \"revised_prompt\": \"## Background\\n\\nSpurTalk is a personal task management app for procrastinators built on the 'Anti-Guilt' standard. The backend is Express + TypeScript + Prisma + PostgreSQL. Services follow a class-based singleton pattern (see "'`backend/src/services/garden.ts`, `backend/src/services/unblocker.ts`). Routes use the `authenticateToken` middleware from `backend/src/middleware/auth.ts`. Shared Zod schemas live in `shared/src/index.ts`. The Prisma schema is at `prisma/schema.prisma`.'"\\n\\nThe app currently has NO proactive communication channel — users must open the app themselves. This M1 milestone builds the first channel: in-app notifications + a background scheduler, so SpurTalk can gently nudge users when they need it.\\n\\n**Core design principle:** Notifications must feel like a calm, encouraging presence — never anxiety-inducing. Think 'garden tending' not 'deadline pressure.'\\n\\n## Directives\\n\\n### 1. Prisma Schema — Add "'`InAppNotification` Model'"\\n\\nAdd to "'`prisma/schema.prisma`:'"\\n\\n"'```prisma'"\\nmodel InAppNotification {\\n  id          String    @id @default(uuid())\\n  userId      String\\n  triggerType String    // \\\"stall\\\" | \\\"deadline\\\" | \\\"daily_checkin\\\" | \\\"streak\\\" | \\\"milestone\\\"\\n  message     String\\n  taskId      String?\\n  deliveredAt DateTime  @default(now()) @map(\\\"delivered_at\\\")\\n  readAt      DateTime? @map(\\\"read_at\\\")\\n  createdAt   DateTime  @default(now()) @map(\\\"created_at\\\")\\n  user        User      @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\\n\\n  @@index([userId, readAt])\\n  @@map(\\\"in_app_notifications\\\")\\n}\\n"'```'"\\n\\nAlso add the relation to the "'`User` model:'"\\n"'```prisma'"\\nmodel User {\\n  // ... existing fields ...\\n  notifications InAppNotification[]\\n}\\n"'```'"\\n\\nThen run "'`npx prisma migrate dev --name add-in-app-notifications`.'"\\n\\n### 2. Scheduler Service\\n\\nCreate "'`backend/src/services/scheduler.ts` following the existing service pattern.'"\\n\\n- Export a "'`SchedulerService` class with a singleton `schedulerService`.'"\\n- Method "'`start()`: sets a `setInterval` (or Node.js timer) that runs every 15 minutes.'"\\n- Method "'`stop()`: clears the interval.'"\\n- Method "'`runEvaluationCycle()`: for each user, evaluates all trigger conditions and dispatches qualifying notifications via the `NotificationService`.'"\\n- The scheduler should respect user quiet hours — do not dispatch during quiet hours; instead queue and deliver at the end of quiet hours.\\n- Each trigger should only fire once per user per task per 24h window (dedup via checking recent "'`InAppNotification` records).'"\\n- Log each cycle run with counts: users evaluated, notifications created, skipped (quiet hours), skipped (dedup).\\n\\n### 3. Trigger System\\n\\nImplement four triggers inside the scheduler evaluation cycle:\\n\\n**3a. Stall Detection Trigger**\\n- Query tasks where "'`state` is `Active` or `Deck` AND `updatedAt` is older than 24 hours AND no stall notification exists for this task in the last 24h.'"\\n- Reuse the stall-detection-timeout from "'`User.preferences.stallDetectionTimeout` (default 24h).'"\\n- Message: 'Hey, no pressure — want to do one nano-step?'\\n- triggerType: "'`'"'stall'"'`'"\\n\\n**3b. Deadline Approaching Trigger**\\n- Query tasks with a "'`hardDeadline` within the next 24 hours AND no deadline notification for this task in the last 24h.'"\\n- Only fire if "'`User.preferences.deadlineAlerts` is not `false`.'"\\n- Message: 'Your deadline is tomorrow. Just one step?'\\n- triggerType: "'`'"'deadline'"'`'"\\n- Edge case: If deadline is past (overdue), do NOT generate a deadline notification (no anxiety).\\n\\n**3c. Daily Check-In Trigger**\\n- Check if current time (in user's timezone from "'`User.preferences.timezone`) matches the user'"'s configured "'`dailyCheckInTime` (default `'"'09:00'"'`).'"\\n- Only fire once per calendar day per user.\\n- Only fire if "'`User.preferences.dailyCheckIn` is not `false`.'"\\n- Message: 'What one thing will you tackle today?'\\n- triggerType: "'`'"'daily_checkin'"'`'"\\n\\n**3d. Streak at Risk Trigger**\\n- Read "'`User.gardenState.currentStreak`. If streak > 0 AND the user has not completed any task today (check tasks with `completedAt` today), the streak is at risk.'"\\n- Only fire once per calendar day per user.\\n- Only fire if "'`User.preferences.streakAlerts` is not `false`.'"\\n- Message: 'Your streak is about to break — 5 min?'\\n- triggerType: "'`'"'streak'"'`'"\\n- Edge case: If streak is already 0, no notification (no shame).\\n\\n**3e. Milestone Trigger (bonus)**\\n- When a user completes a task, check if it's their Nth task (e.g., 1st, 5th, 10th, 25th, 50th, 100th). If so, create a milestone notification.\\n- triggerType: "'`'"'milestone'"'`'"\\n- Message: '🎉 You did it"'!'"'\\n- This can be triggered from the existing task completion flow rather than the scheduler.\\n\\n### 4. Notification Service\\n\\nCreate "'`backend/src/services/notification.ts`:'"\\n\\n- "'`createNotification(userId, triggerType, message, taskId?)` — inserts an `InAppNotification` record.'"\\n- "'`getNotifications(userId, options?)` — returns user'"'s notifications, unread first, with pagination (default limit 50).\\n- "'`markAsRead(userId, notificationId)` — sets `readAt` to now. Returns 404 if not found or not owned by user.'"\\n- "'`markAllAsRead(userId)` — marks all unread notifications as read for a user.'"\\n- "'`isInQuietHours(userId)` — reads user'"'s "'`communicationPreferences.quietHours` and checks if current time (in user timezone) falls within quiet hours.'"\\n- "'`shouldDedup(userId, triggerType, taskId?)` — checks if a notification of this type for this task already exists within the last 24h.'"\\n\\n### 5. Message Templates\\n\\nCreate "'`backend/src/services/messageTemplates.ts`:'"\\n\\nDefine all message templates in one place. Every message must use nurturing, non-judgmental language. No alarms, no urgent colors, no shame.\\n\\n"'```typescript'"\\nconst MESSAGE_TEMPLATES = {\\n  stall: 'Hey, no pressure — want to do one nano-step?',\\n  deadline: 'Your deadline is tomorrow. Just one step?',\\n  daily_checkin: 'What one thing will you tackle today?',\\n  streak: 'Your streak is about to break — 5 min?',\\n  milestone: '🎉 You did it"'!'"',\\n} as const;\\n"'```'"\\n\\nAlso define a "'`formatMessage(template, context?)` function that allows inserting task title or other context when appropriate.'"\\n\\n### 6. User Communication Preferences\\n\\nExtend "'`User.preferences` JSON field. The existing `UserPreferencesSchema` in `shared/src/index.ts` already has a `notificationSettings` object with `taskReminders`, `stallDetection`, and `milestoneCelebrations`. Extend it with communication-specific preferences:'"\\n\\n"'```typescript'"\\ncommunicationPreferences: z.object({\\n  channels: z.array(z.enum(['in_app'])).default(['in_app']),\\n  quietHours: z.object({\\n    start: z.string().regex(/"'^'"\\\\d{2}:\\\\d{2}"'$/).default('"'22:00'),\\n    end: z.string().regex(/"'^'"\\\\d{2}:\\\\d{2}"'$/).default('"'08:00'),\\n  }).default({ start: '22:00', end: '08:00' }),\\n  dailyCheckInTime: z.string().regex(/"'^'"\\\\d{2}:\\\\d{2}"'$/).default('"'09:00'),\\n  stallAlerts: z.boolean().default(true),\\n  deadlineAlerts: z.boolean().default(true),\\n  dailyCheckIn: z.boolean().default(true),\\n  streakAlerts: z.boolean().default(true),\\n}).default({\\n  channels: ['in_app'],\\n  quietHours: { start: '22:00', end: '08:00' },\\n  dailyCheckInTime: '09:00',\\n  stallAlerts: true,\\n  deadlineAlerts: true,\\n  dailyCheckIn: true,\\n  streakAlerts: true,\\n})\\n"'```'"\\n\\nMigrate the existing "'`notificationSettings` into this new `communicationPreferences` structure, or keep both and have the scheduler read from `communicationPreferences` with fallback to `notificationSettings` for backward compatibility.'"\\n\\n### 7. API Endpoints\\n\\nCreate "'`backend/src/routes/notifications.ts`:'"\\n\\n**GET /api/notifications**\\n- Requires "'`authenticateToken`'"\\n- Query params: "'`?unread=true` (filter to unread only), `?limit=50`, `?offset=0`'"\\n- Returns notifications sorted by "'`createdAt` DESC, unread first'"\\n- Response: "'`{ notifications: InAppNotification[], total: number, unread: number }`'"\\n\\n**PATCH /api/notifications/:id/read**\\n- Requires "'`authenticateToken`'"\\n- Marks a single notification as read\\n- Returns updated notification\\n- 404 if not found or not owned by user\\n- 400 if already read\\n\\n**PATCH /api/notifications/read-all**\\n- Requires "'`authenticateToken`'"\\n- Marks all unread notifications as read for the authenticated user\\n- Returns "'`{ updated: number }`'"\\n\\n**GET /api/users/me/communication-preferences**\\n- Requires "'`authenticateToken`'"\\n- Returns the user's "'`communicationPreferences` from `User.preferences`'"\\n\\n**PATCH /api/users/me/communication-preferences**\\n- Requires "'`authenticateToken`'"\\n- Validates body against the communication preferences schema\\n- Merges with existing preferences (partial update)\\n- Returns updated preferences\\n\\n### 8. Wire Up in "'`backend/src/index.ts`'"\\n\\n- Import and mount notification routes: "'`app.use('"'/api/notifications', notificationRoutes)"'`'"\\n- Start the scheduler on server boot (non-test environments): call "'`schedulerService.start()`'"\\n- Graceful shutdown: call "'`schedulerService.stop()` on SIGTERM/SIGINT'"\\n\\n### 9. Tests\\n\\nCreate "'`backend/src/test/notifications.test.ts` and `backend/src/test/scheduler.test.ts`:'"\\n\\n- Unit tests for "'`NotificationService` (create, get, markAsRead, markAllAsRead, quiet hours, dedup)'"\\n- Unit tests for each trigger condition (stall, deadline, daily check-in, streak, milestone)\\n- Unit tests for quiet hours logic (cross-midnight quiet hours, e.g., 22:00-08:00)\\n- Unit tests for dedup logic (no duplicate notifications within 24h)\\n- Integration tests for API endpoints (GET /api/notifications, PATCH read, PATCH read-all, GET/PATCH preferences)\\n- Test that messages use nurturing language (no 'overdue', 'urgent', 'fail' words)\\n- Run with: "'`cd backend && npm test`'"\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n- Follow existing service class + singleton export pattern (see "'`gardenService`, `unblockerService`)'"\\n- Use "'`authenticateToken` middleware for all notification endpoints'"\\n- Use Zod for request validation (see existing "'`CreateTaskSchema` pattern)'"\\n- Use "'`@spurtalk/shared` for shared types and schemas'"\\n- No external notification services for M1 — everything stays in-process\\n- No Redis/BullMQ for M1 — use "'`setInterval` for the scheduler (can be upgraded later)'"\\n- The scheduler must not block the Express event loop — use "'`setImmediate` or process users in batches'"\\n- All database access through Prisma client (see "'`backend/src/lib/prisma.ts`)'"\\n- Never use anxiety-inducing language in any message template\\n- Never send notifications during user's configured quiet hours\\n- Never send duplicate notifications (dedup within 24h per trigger+task per user)\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n1. "'`cd /Users/morsy/dev/spurtalk && npx prisma migrate dev --name add-in-app-notifications` — migration applies cleanly'"\\n2. "'`cd /Users/morsy/dev/spurtalk/backend && npm run typecheck` — no TypeScript errors'"\\n3. "'`cd /Users/morsy/dev/spurtalk/backend && npm test` — all tests pass'"\\n4. "'`cd /Users/morsy/dev/spurtalk/backend && npm run dev` — server starts, scheduler logs '"'Scheduler started' message\\n5. Manual: "'`GET /api/notifications` returns 200 with notification list'"\\n6. Manual: "'`PATCH /api/notifications/:id/read` marks notification as read'"\\n7. Manual: "'`GET /api/users/me/communication-preferences` returns preferences'"\\n8. Manual: "'`PATCH /api/users/me/communication-preferences` updates preferences",
